                <pb facs="0421" n="307" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg307"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">875.00/133: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Fletcher</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-06-02T20:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 2, 1924—8
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 8:45 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>104. I am just notified by the Foreign Office that as communication with Durazzo
                    is interrupted an Italian destroyer is being sent immediately to Durazzo. In
                    accordance with desire of Minister Tirana I have just relayed his request for a
                    destroyer to the naval attaché at Athens.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fletcher</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
